  ('killington-vermont', '12A', 'Killington', 'United States', 'The Beast of the East', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'New England', '{"ski","entertainment","culinary","family","adventure","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Killington = ''The Beast of the East'', the LARGEST ski area in the eastern US; six interconnected peaks (Killington, Snowdon, Skye, Ramshead, Bear, Sunrise); 1,509 acres, 155 trails (212 incl affiliated Pico Mountain, same pass)","New England''s BIGGEST vertical (3,050 ft) off a 4,229-ft summit (Killington Peak; 2nd-highest in the Green Mtns); base 1,165 ft; K-1 Express + Skyeship gondolas among 21 lifts; ~250 in snow + ~71% snowmaking","LONGEST SEASON IN THE EAST: typically late Oct-late May (200+ days), first open (October) + last to close (Superstar into May/June via snowmaking); the ''King of Spring''","OWNERSHIP CORRECTED: no longer Powdr - bought by the local Killington Independence Group on 27 Sep 2024 (Powdr retained a minority stake); on the Ikon Pass (Beast 365 Pass includes Ikon Base; full-Ikon upgrade available)","Stifel Killington Cup = FIS Alpine WORLD CUP (women''s GS + slalom) on Superstar every Thanksgiving weekend since 2016 (one of few US World Cup races; Shiffrin won slalom the first 5 editions); FIS confirms 28-29 Nov 2026","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: among the most-visited Eastern resorts but no per-resort count published - consensus only","Killington Road (''the Access Road'') = a genuine apres/nightlife strip (The Wobbly Barn); closest commercial airport Rutland (RUT, Cape Air to Boston ~40 min); Boston + NY/NJ drive market; ~15 mi from Rutland","NO on-site cat/heli (fully lift-served); NO natural hot springs (none in region); NO avalanche center (low-avalanche Eastern terrain - ice/cold/driving spine); MID-MARKET (not ultra-luxury); Ikon/lift prices dynamic; summer bike park + golf + Beast Mountain Coaster"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/