  ('timberline-mt-hood-oregon', '12A', 'Timberline Lodge / Mt. Hood', 'United States', 'The only place in America you can ski every', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Pacific Northwest', '{"ski","ultra","romance","culinary","family","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["The only year-round ski area in the US — Palmer Snowfield/Glacier lift-served ~Jun-Aug (Palmer upper terminal ~8,500 ft; base/lodge ~5,960-6,000 ft)","Official SUMMER training site of the US Ski & Snowboard Teams (GS, slalom, moguls, skier/snowboardcross + World Cup start gate) + Freestyle Training Center; biggest summer camp scene in North America","Timberline Lodge = National Historic Landmark, built 1936-38 by the WPA, dedicated by FDR 28 Sept 1937; Overlook Hotel exterior in ''The Shining'' (1980)","Independent — Mt. Hood Fusion Pass (Timberline + Summit Pass + Skibowl, Powder Alliance); NOT Epic/Ikon","Mt. Hood = active glaciated stratovolcano (summit 11,249 ft); Palmer glaciated — crevasse hazard above the lift","~60 mi east of Portland on US-26 (Government Camp); PDX ~1.5 hr; NWAC covers the zone; nearest hospitals Providence Hood River / Legacy Mount Hood Medical Center (Gresham)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide)","hospital":"on-mountain ski patrol in season; nearest hospitals Providence Hood River Memorial + Legacy Mount Hood Medical Center (Gresham, 24/7 ER); serious cases to Portland trauma centers; summit rescue via Clackamas County Sheriff + Portland Mountain Rescue / 911","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"UPPER-MOUNTAIN EXPOSURE + FAST WHITEOUT (Hood notorious; 1986 OES tragedy) turn back early; GLACIER/CREVASSE hazard on Palmer + summit (11,249 ft = roped guided mountaineering only); AVALANCHE beyond ropes (check NWAC, guide + beacon/probe/shovel); Cascade winter driving + ODOT chain control (US-26/TripCheck); moderate altitude (base ~5,96